# Not needed locally: local dev, tests and `npm run verify` use none of these (without SENTRY_DSN,
# Sentry stays off). They are injected at build time by the "Build and Deploy" GitHub Actions
# workflow, which also uploads source maps to Sentry (together with SENTRY_UPLOAD=true). Listed here
# for reference only:
#   SENTRY_DSN         repository variable (public: it ships in the bundle, so not a secret)
#   SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN  secret on the "production" environment
#   SENTRY_ORG         repository variable
#   SENTRY_PROJECT     repository variable
# The build reads real environment variables, not this file (there is no .env loading): to try
# Sentry in dev, run e.g. `SENTRY_DSN=<dsn> npm run dev`.
SENTRY_DSN=
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
SENTRY_ORG=
SENTRY_PROJECT=
